+//
+// Scope, stated plainly: this does NOT validate any offset against Minecraft. No libminecraftpe.so was
+// available, so binary validation remains PENDING for every value here. What this does guarantee is the
+// thing centralisation could otherwise silently break - that moving the five literals out of
+// Hologram.cpp into lm::off preserved each value exactly. The right-hand sides below are the literals as
+// they appeared at their use sites before Phase 0; if anyone edits a centralised constant, the
+// static_assert fails at compile time instead of the offset drifting unnoticed.
